n\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n8278,YOGUR,\"Yogur is a dairy product that is recognized for its numerous health benefits and dietary versatility. It is a food item that is often included in a moderate low-sodium diet and serves as a dessert option in various meal plans. Yogur undergoes fermentation, a process that involves bacteria that help to partially hydrolyze lactose, making it more tolerable for individuals who are lactose intolerant. This fermentation process not only improves lactose digestion but also enhances the overall nutritional profile of the yogurt.\n\nYogur contains 2.2 mg of iron per 100 grams and has a glycemic index of 51, indicating its moderate impact on blood sugar levels. It is also a good source of calcium, which is essential for bone health, and is recommended for daily intake. Additionally, yogur is beneficial for gut health, particularly during episodes of diarrhea, as it contains probiotics that support digestive function.\n\nFurthermore, yogur is a soft food option suitable for patients with dysphagia, although caution is advised when mixing it with fruits due to potential risks. Overall, yogur is a nutritious and versatile food that can be enjoyed by a wide range of individuals, contributing positively to their dietary needs.\",6\r\n9560,LACTASA,\"LACTASA is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the digestion of lactose, a sugar found in milk and dairy products. It hydrolyzes lactose into its constituent sugars, glucose and galactose, which are essential for energy derived from milk carbohydrates in mammals. A deficiency in lactase is commonly observed in patients with celiac disease, leading to lactose intolerance. Although lactase is not inducible, its production can adapt with continuous consumption of lactose, allowing some individuals to better digest lactose over time.\",9\r\n14001,INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS,\"INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS refer to adverse reactions to certain foods that do not involve the immune system, distinguishing them from food allergies. These intolerances are often linked to enzyme deficiencies, such as lactose intolerance, where the body lacks the necessary enzymes to properly digest specific foods. The reactions associated with food intolerances are non-immune and can lead to various symptoms, particularly gastrointestinal issues, as well as other health problems. In summary, INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS are characterized by their non-IgE mediated nature, resulting in a range of adverse effects without the involvement of the immune response.\",10\r\n9477,LACTOSA,\"LACTOSA is a disaccharide sugar composed of glucose and galactose, primarily found in milk and dairy products. It plays a significant role in nutrition but can lead to lactose intolerance in some individuals. Lactose intolerance is a condition where the body is unable to properly digest lactose, resulting in various gastrointestinal symptoms. This condition can affect individuals with malabsorption issues, including those with specific gastrointestinal diseases such as Crohn's disease, particularly during flare-ups.\n\nIn addition to its presence in milk, lactose is also found in various packaged foods, where it may be used as a preservative. For individuals with dietary restrictions, such as those with fructose malabsorption or certain metabolic disorders like Glycogen Storage Disease Type I (GSDI), it is important to limit lactose intake. Overall, while lactose is a common component of many foods, its impact on digestion varies among individuals, necessitating careful dietary considerations for those affected by lactose intolerance.\",18\r\n9478,GALACTOSA,\"Galactosa is a monosaccharide that plays a crucial role in the diet of mammals, primarily found in milk and its derivatives. It is a component of lactose and is significant in various metabolic processes. However, galactosa is a simple sugar that can be metabolized in the body, and in certain conditions, it may accumulate, leading to toxicity. This accumulation can pose risks, particularly in individuals with specific metabolic disorders. For instance, when administered, galactosa does not improve hypoglycemia in patients with type I glycogen storage disease (GSDI) and may even exacerbate acidosis. Additionally, it is advised that children with GSDI limit their intake of galactosa. Furthermore, ingestion of galactosa can lead to complications in patients with classic galactosemia, a genetic disorder that impairs the metabolism of this sugar. Overall, while galactosa is an important dietary component, its management is critical in certain medical conditions.\",12\r\n9028,SISTEMA INMUNE,\"El sistema inmune es el conjunto de células y mecanismos que protegen al organismo contra infecciones y enfermedades, incluyendo reacciones alérgicas. Este sistema es fundamental para la defensa del cuerpo y su desarrollo en niños puede influir en la prevalencia de alergias. Además, el sistema inmune es una red compleja de células y proteínas que defiende al organismo contra infecciones, y su desarrollo y mantenimiento están influenciados por la microbiota intestinal. Cambios en esta microbiota, como los provocados por el uso de antibióticos, pueden afectar el funcionamiento del sistema inmune.\",6\r\n9026,ALERGIAS,\"Alergias refer to allergies, which are immune system reactions to specific substances. These reactions can be influenced by various factors, including genetic predispositions and environmental conditions. Additionally, changes in microbiota due to antibiotic use may also play a role in the development of allergies. Among the different types of allergies, food allergies are notable as they represent adverse immune responses to certain foods. These food allergies can manifest in early childhood and may vary in duration and severity over time.\",11\r\n9735,ENZYMATIC ACTIVITY,\"The measurement of enzymatic activity is crucial for diagnosing lactose intolerance, particularly through biopsies.\",2\r\n9763,TEST DE HIDRÓGENO ESPIRADO,\"The \"\"TEST DE HIDRÓGENO ESPIRADO\"\" is a diagnostic method utilized to assess various gastrointestinal conditions. Primarily, it is employed to diagnose lactose intolerance by measuring the amount of hydrogen present in the breath following the ingestion of lactose. Additionally, the test serves as a tool to confirm glucose-galactose malabsorption by evaluating hydrogen levels after the consumption of sugar. This dual application highlights the test's significance in identifying different types of carbohydrate malabsorption issues.\",2\r\n14060,BIOPSIA DE INTESTINO DELGADO,\"La biopsia de intestino delgado es un procedimiento invasivo que puede confirmar la intolerancia a la lactosa tras un test positivo, aunque no es comúnmente utilizado.\",1\r\n12370,FLORA INTESTINAL,\"Intestinal flora refers to the community of microorganisms in the gut, which can be altered in patients with EII and affect lactose digestion.\",1\r\n14059,TEST DE TOLERANCIA A LA LACTOSA,\"El test de tolerancia a la lactosa mide la respuesta glucémica tras la ingestión de lactosa, ayudando a diagnosticar la deficiencia de lactasa.\",1\r\n14061,PCR DEL GEN DE LA LACTASA,\"La PCR del gen de la lactasa es una prueba genética que ayuda a diferenciar entre hipolactasia primaria y secundaria, aunque no está disponible en la práctica clínica habitual.\",1\r\n9549,GALACTOSA-1-FOSFATO URIDIL TRANSFERASA,\"Galactosa-1-fosfato uridil transferasa (GALT) is an enzyme that converts galactose-1-phosphate and uridine diphosphate glucose into uridine diphosphate galactose and glucose-1-phosphate, and is expressed by the GALT gene on chromosome 9p13.\",2\r\n9551,ÁCIDO GALACTÓNICO,\"Ácido galactónico is a metabolite that is formed from galactose and plays a crucial role in the metabolism of galactose. It is produced through the action of the enzyme galactose dehydrogenase and can be utilized in alternative metabolic pathways. This compound is integral to the overall process of galactose metabolization, highlighting its importance in biochemical processes related to this sugar.\",2\r\n14020,MEDIO AMBIENTE,\"El medio ambiente se refiere a las condiciones externas que pueden influir en la salud y predisposición a enfermedades, incluyendo alergias.\",2\r\n9552,VÍA LELOIR,\"The Leloir pathway is a metabolic pathway that converts galactose into glucose, involving several enzymatic steps and is crucial for proper carbohydrate metabolism.\",1\r\n14021,POLIMORFISMOS,\"Los polimorfismos son variaciones en el ADN que pueden influir en la predisposición a enfermedades, incluyendo alergias alimentarias.\",1\r\n14062,SENSIBILIZACIÓN,\"La sensibilización es el proceso por el cual el sistema inmunológico se vuelve reactivo a ciertos alérgenos, comúnmente ocurriendo en los primeros años de vida.\",1\r\n14066,PROBLEMAS DERMATOLÓGICOS,Los problemas dermatológicos son afecciones de la piel que pueden estar relacionadas con alergias o intolerancias alimentarias.,1\r\n14067,SOCIETADES CIENTÍFICAS DE ALERGOLOGÍA,Las sociedades científicas de alergología son organizaciones que estudian y promueven el conocimiento sobre alergias e intolerancias alimentarias.,1\r\n14065,TRASTORNOS GASTROINTESTINALES,Los trastornos gastrointestinales son condiciones que afectan el sistema digestivo y pueden ser tratados o diagnosticados mediante pruebas de intolerancia alimentaria.,1\r\n14068,SOCIETADES CIENTÍFICAS DE NUTRICIÓN,\"Las sociedades científicas de nutrición son organizaciones que investigan y educan sobre la relación entre la alimentación y la salud, incluyendo alergias e intolerancias.\",1\r\n9716,AFRICA,\"Africa has a high prevalence of lactose intolerance, ranging from 65-75%.\",1\r\n9717,ASIA,\"Asia has the highest prevalence of lactose intolerance, exceeding 90%.\",1\r\n9718,NATIVE AMERICANS,\"Native Americans have a very high prevalence of lactose intolerance, estimated at 90-95%.\",1\r\n9722,PERIODO PERINATAL,\"El período perinatal es el tiempo alrededor del nacimiento, donde la expresión de lactasa aumenta.\",1\r\n9027,DIVERSIDAD FILOGENÉTICA,\"Diversidad filogenética refers to the genetic diversity of microbial communities, which can be altered by antibiotic treatment.\",1\r\n9025,INFECCIONES BACTERIANAS,\"Infecciones bacterianas refer to bacterial infections that antibiotics are used to treat, which can impact microbiota diversity.\",1\r\n9736,GENETIC STUDY,Genetic studies are conducted to identify mutations in the LCT gene associated with lactose intolerance.,1\r\n9554,GALACTOSA DESHIDROGENASA,\"Galactosa deshidrogenasa, also known as galactose dehydrogenase, is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the metabolism of galactose. It catalyzes the oxidation of galactose, converting it into ácido galactónico (galactonic acid). This enzymatic reaction is an important step in the metabolic pathway of galactose, facilitating its proper utilization in biological processes.\",1\r\n9553,GEN GALT,\"The GALT gene is responsible for encoding the enzyme galactose-1-phosphate uridil transferase, and mutations in this gene can lead to galactosemia.\",1\r\n14022,GENOMA,,1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n17063,YOGUR,NUTRICIÓN PEDIÁTRICA,Yogur is recommended as a source of iron in pediatric nutrition,168\r\n8258,CALCIO,YOGUR,\"CALCIO and YOGUR are closely related, particularly in the context of dietary recommendations. Yogur, commonly known as yogurt, is frequently recommended as a beneficial source of c