n17695,LACTOSA,INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS,\"LACTOSA is a specific type of food intolerance that affects many individuals, particularly adults who have difficulty absorbing this sugar. This condition, known as lactose intolerance, is a common form of food intolerance that can lead to various digestive issues when lactose-containing foods are consumed.\",28\r\n17707,GALACTOSA,GALACTOSEMIA CLÁSICA,La ingesta de galactosa causa complicaciones en pacientes con galactosemia clásica.,27\r\n17677,GSDI,GALACTOSA,Galactose should be restricted in the diet of children with GSDI to maintain stable glucose levels.,27\r\n17690,LACTOSA,LACTASA,\"LACTOSA and LACTASA are closely related entities in the context of lactose metabolism. LACTASA, also known as lactase, is the enzyme responsible for breaking down LACTOSA, which is a sugar found in milk and dairy products. This enzymatic action converts LACTOSA into glucose and galactose, two simpler sugars that can be easily absorbed by the body. The relevance of LACTASA is particularly significant for individuals with lactose intolerance, a condition where the body lacks sufficient lactase to properly digest lactose, leading to various digestive issues. Thus, LACTASA plays a crucial role in the digestion of LACTOSA, highlighting the importance of this enzyme in maintaining digestive health for those who consume dairy products.\",27\r\n16905,GLUTEN,INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS,\"El gluten puede causar sensibilidad en algunas personas, lo que se relaciona con intolerancias alimentarias.\",26\r\n15710,EUROPE,LACTASA,\"In Europe, particularly in northern and western regions, there is a higher prevalence of lactase persistence.\",26\r\n4312,ENFERMEDAD,ALERGIAS,Las alergias son consideradas enfermedades que afectan la salud y pueden ser influenciadas por factores genéticos y ambientales.,25\r\n16875,FRUCTOSA,INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS,\"La fructosa puede causar intolerancia en algunas personas, lo que la convierte en un tipo de intolerancia alimentaria.\",24\r\n17062,YOGUR,LACTOSA,\"YOGUR is a dairy product that contains beneficial bacteria which ferment lactosa, thereby reducing its overall content. This fermentation process not only diminishes the amount of lactosa present in the yogurt but also enhances the tolerance of individuals who may have difficulty digesting this sugar. As a result, yogurt is often well-tolerated by lactose-intolerant individuals, making it a suitable dairy option for those suffering from conditions such as EII (Inflammatory Bowel Disease).\",24\r\n9494,INTESTINO DELGADO,GALACTOSA,\"In the intestino delgado, galactosa is digested with the help of specific enzymes\",22\r\n16845,MANTEQUILLA,LACTOSA,\"MANTEQUILLA, commonly known as butter, is often associated with lactose content. However, there is a notable distinction regarding its suitability for individuals with lactose intolerance. While it is true that butter contains lactose, the process of making MANTEQUILLA involves the separation of its components, which results in a product that typically contains very low levels of lactose. This makes MANTEQUILLA generally acceptable for many people with lactose intolerance. In contrast, LACTOSA, or lactose, is a sugar found in milk and dairy products that can cause discomfort for those who are intolerant. Therefore, while MANTEQUILLA may contain trace amounts of LACTOSA, it is often considered safe for consumption by individuals who are lactose intolerant due to the minimal lactose content resulting from its production process.\",22\r\n17410,ALERGIAS,INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS,\"ALERGIAS and INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS are both types of adverse reactions to food. However, they differ significantly in their underlying mechanisms. Alergias are mediated by the immune system, which means they involve an immune response to certain food proteins. In contrast, intolerancias alimentarias do not involve the immune system; instead, they typically result from the body's inability to properly digest or metabolize certain foods. Additionally, the symptoms associated with these two conditions can vary, reflecting their distinct mechanisms.\",21\r\n17691,LACTOSA,ENZYMATIC ACTIVITY,The measurement of enzymatic activity is essential for diagnosing issues related to lactose consumption.,20\r\n17883,SÍNDROME DE INTESTINO IRRITABLE,INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS,\"Síndrome de intestino irritable can be influenced by food intolerances, leading to gastrointestinal symptoms\",20\r\n17696,LACTOSA,TEST DE HIDRÓGENO ESPIRADO,\"El test de hidrógeno espirado se utiliza para diagnosticar la intolerancia a la lactosa, midiendo la producción de hidrógeno tras la ingestión de lactosa.\",20\r\n17698,LACTOSA,BIOPSIA DE INTESTINO DELGADO,\"La biopsia de intestino delgado puede confirmar la intolerancia a la lactosa tras un test positivo, aunque es un método invasivo.\",19\r\n17694,LACTOSA,FLORA INTESTINAL,Alterations in intestinal flora can impact the digestion of lactose in patients with EII,19\r\n17708,GALACTOSA,GLUCOGENOSIS DE TIPO I,Galactosa does not improve hypoglycemia in glucogenosis de tipo I and may worsen acidosis,19\r\n17697,LACTOSA,TEST DE TOLERANCIA A LA LACTOSA,\"El test de tolerancia a la lactosa se utiliza para evaluar la capacidad del cuerpo para procesar lactosa, ayudando a diagnosticar la intolerancia.\",19\r\n17699,LACTOSA,PCR DEL GEN DE LA LACTASA,\"La PCR del gen de la lactasa puede ayudar a diferenciar entre tipos de hipolactasia, aunque no es comúnmente utilizada en la práctica clínica.\",19\r\n9614,HLA,ALERGIAS,Los polimorfismos en las regiones HLA están relacionados con la predisposición genética a las alergias alimentarias.,18\r\n17703,GALACTOSA,GALACTITOL,\"Galactose can be converted into galactitol through the action of aldose reductase, which is an alternative metabolic pathway.\",18\r\n17409,ALERGIAS,SISTEMA INMUNE,\"Allergies are closely related to the immune system, which plays a crucial role in the body's response to allergens. The development of the immune system in children is a key factor influencing their susceptibility to food allergies. Additionally, changes in microbiota due to antibiotic use can impact the immune system, further affecting the likelihood of developing allergies.\",17\r\n17705,GALACTOSA,GALACTOKINASA,\"Galactokinase phosphorylates galactose to initiate its metabolism, establishing a direct relationship.\",17\r\n17951,MALABSORCIÓN DE GLUCOSA-GALACTOSA,TEST DE HIDRÓGENO ESPIRADO,The hydrogen breath test is used to diagnose glucose-galactose malabsorption,16\r\n17414,ALERGIAS,ALERGENO,\"Los alérgenos son las sustancias que provocan reacciones alérgicas, siendo un componente clave en el estudio de las alergias alimentarias.\",15\r\n17061,YOGUR,DBIG,\"Yogur is an example of a food with a moderate glycemic index, which is relevant to the principles of DBIG\",15\r\n17702,GALACTOSA,GALACTOSA-1-FOSFATO URIDIL TRANSFERASA,\"Galactose is a substrate for the enzyme galactose-1-phosphate uridil transferase, which converts it into uridine diphosphate galactose.\",14\r\n17704,GALACTOSA,ÁCIDO GALACTÓNICO,\"Galactose is metabolized to galactonic acid via the action of galactose dehydrogenase, which is part of its metabolic pathway.\",14\r\n7322,SÍNTOMAS GASTROINTESTINALES,INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS,\"Las intolerancias alimentarias pueden causar síntomas gastrointestinales, que son una manifestación común de estas condiciones.\",14\r\n17411,ALERGIAS,MEDIO AMBIENTE,El medio ambiente puede afectar la prevalencia y severidad de las alergias alimentarias.,13\r\n17706,GALACTOSA,VÍA LELOIR,\"The Leloir pathway is the metabolic route through which galactose is converted into glucose, establishing a strong relationship.\",13\r\n17787,LACTASA,LCT,\"Lactasa is encoded by the LCT gene, which is responsible for lactose digestion.\",13\r\n17412,ALERGIAS,POLIMORFISMOS,Los polimorfismos en el ADN pueden influir en la predisposición a desarrollar alergias alimentarias.,12\r\n17413,ALERGIAS,SENSIBILIZACIÓN,\"La sensibilización es un proceso que puede llevar a la aparición de alergias alimentarias, especialmente en los primeros años de vida.\",12\r\n17415,ALERGIAS,PROBLEMAS DERMATOLÓGICOS,\"Los problemas dermatológicos pueden ser una manifestación de alergias alimentarias, mostrando la conexión entre la piel y la dieta.\",12\r\n17416,ALERGIAS,SOCIETADES CIENTÍFICAS DE ALERGOLOGÍA,Las sociedades científicas de alergología investigan y proporcionan información sobre las alergias alimentarias y su manejo.,12\r\n19747,INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS,TRASTORNOS GASTROINTESTINALES,\"Los trastornos gastrointestinales pueden ser síntomas de intolerancias alimentarias, afectando la calidad de vida de los pacientes.\",11\r\n19748,INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS,SOCIETADES CIENTÍFICAS DE NUTRICIÓN,\"Las sociedades científicas de nutrición estudian la relación entre la dieta y las intolerancias alimentarias, promoviendo prácticas saludables.\",11\r\n17788,LACTASA,AFRICA,\"Africa has a high prevalence of lactose intolerance, indicating lower lactase persistence.\",10\r\n17789,LACTASA,ASIA,\"Asia has the highest prevalence of lactose intolerance, indicating very low lactase persistence.\",10\r\n17790,LACTASA,NATIVE AMERICANS,\"Native Americans have a very high prevalence of lactose intolerance, indicating low lactase persistence.\",10\r\n17791,LACTASA,PERIODO PERINATAL,\"La expresión de lactasa aumenta durante el período perinatal, lo que es crucial para la digestión de la leche en los mamíferos.\",10\r\n17417,DIVERSIDAD FILOGENÉTICA,SISTEMA INMUNE,Changes in phylogenetic diversity can affect the immune system's response,7\r\n17408,INFECCIONES BACTERIANAS,SISTEMA INMUNE,\"Bacterial infections can impact the immune system, which may be influenced by antibiotic use\",7\r\n17934,ENZYMATIC ACTIVITY,GENETIC STUDY,Genetic studies help determine the underlying causes of enzymatic activity related to lactose intolerance.,3\r\n17782,ÁCIDO GALACTÓNICO,GALACTOSA DESHIDROGENASA,\"Galactose dehydrogenase catalyzes the conversion of galactose to galactonic acid, linking these two entities in the metabolic pathway.\",3\r\n17777,GALACTOSA-1-FOSFATO URIDIL TRANSFERASA,GEN GALT,\"The GALT gene encodes the enzyme galactose-1-phosphate uridil transferase, which is crucial for galactose metabolism.\",3\r\n19751,MEDIO AMBIENTE,GENOMA,\"El genoma y el medio ambiente interactúan para influir en la predisposición a enfermedades, incluyendo alergias.\",3\r\n\n\nThe report should include the following sections:\n\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant information associated with its entities.\n- IMPACT SEVERITY RATING: a float score between 0-10 that represents the severity of IMPACT posed by entities within the community.  IMPACT is the scored importance of a community.\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the IMPACT severity rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format:\n    {{\n        \"title\": <report_title>,\n        \"summary\": <executive_summary>,\n        \"rating\": <impact_severity_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": <rating_explanation>,\n        \"findings\": [\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_1_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_1_explanation>\n            }},\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_2_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data refe